+# Level‑4 Run Playbook — One Page
+
+Purpose
+- Execute the full production proofs, validate acceptance criteria, generate remediation tickets, and (if ready and legally approved) perform a controlled Gatekeeper promotion toward Level‑4.
+
+Prereqs (operator)
+- kubectl configured to target cluster with Tekton installed
+- AWS CLI configured or IRSA access allowing S3 writes to evidence bucket
+- gh CLI authenticated (for dispatch & issue creation) OR GITHUB_TOKEN set for curl dispatch
+- cosign keys accessible to signing tasks if required
+- Ensure repository contains: ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pr_ready.yaml
+
+Key environment
+- EVIDENCE_BUCKET (example): s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+- REPO (example): rsinghunjan/aegis
+- ASSIGNEE (for auto-created issues): rsinghunjan
+
+Quick run (Tekton in‑cluster)
+1) Ensure the prefilled PipelineRun is correct:
+   - Review ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pr_ready.yaml and confirm `evidence_bucket` is `s3://aegis-evidence-prod`.
+2) Apply:
+   kubectl apply -f ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pr_ready.yaml
+3) Monitor:
+   kubectl -n cicd get pipelineruns -w
+   kubectl -n cicd logs <task-pod> -c <step-name>
+
+Quick run (GitHub Actions dispatch)
+ - Use the provided dispatch script:
+   ./ops/ci/dispatch_ready.sh
+ - Or run (gh CLI):
+   gh workflow run "Execute Production Proofs Now" -R rsinghunjan/aegis --field evidence_bucket="s3://aegis-evidence-prod" --field confirm=RUN_PROOFS
+ - Or use curl (requires GITHUB_TOKEN):
+   See ops/ci/dispatch_ready.sh for the exact curl payload.
+
+Post-run validator checklist (fetch final summary first)
+1) Fetch orchestrator summary (example):
+   aws s3 ls s3://aegis-evidence-prod/production_proofs/
+   aws s3 cp s3://aegis-evidence-prod/production_proofs/final-summary-<ts>.json /tmp/acceptance.json
+2) Run validators (examples):
+   python3 services/hpo/checkpoint_analyzer.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod --threshold 0.90
+   python3 services/telemetry/otel_span_coverage_checker.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+   python3 services/decisioning/opa_full_harness_runner.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+   python3 services/failure/remediation_analyzer.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod --threshold 0.90
+   python3 services/explainability/manifest_index_and_attach.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+   python3 services/reliability/longterm_collection_aggregator.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+
+Generate remediation backlog & optionally create issues
+ - Generate backlog:
+   python3 ops/scripts/generate_remediation_tickets.py --input /tmp/acceptance.json --out /tmp/remediation_backlog.md
+ - Create GitHub issues (requires gh auth):
+   python3 ops/scripts/generate_remediation_tickets.py --input /tmp/acceptance.json --out /tmp/remediation_backlog.md --create-issues --repo rsinghunjan/aegis --assignee rsinghunjan
+ - Or use wrapper:
+   ./ops/scripts/create_remediation_issues.sh --input /tmp/acceptance.json
+
+Compute readiness and promote (guarded)
+1) Compute readiness:
+   export EVIDENCE_BUCKET=s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+   python3 ops/production/readiness_calculator.py
+2) Upload Legal signoff marker when Legal approves:
+   echo "legal ok - $(date -u)" > /tmp/legal_ok.txt
+   aws s3 cp /tmp/legal_ok.txt s3://aegis-evidence-prod/compliance/legal_signoff.txt
+3) Promote when readiness >= threshold:
+   ./ops/production/promote_to_level4.sh --min-readiness 85 --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+
+Rollback & safety notes
+- Promotion script performs a controlled Gatekeeper rollout and uploads verification artifacts. It does NOT perform Terraform apply.
+- If a validator fails, follow backlog items, remediate, re-run the targeted validator(s), then re-run the full proofs.
+
+Contact
+- For questions: @rsinghunjan (repo owner / assignee)
+
